摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Use DeepSeek Harness from your phone or another computer. Host: mobile UI, pairing-code gateway, PWA and Web Push, plus sharing chosen sessions. Client: those sessions appear in another DSH desktop's sidebar. 手机和另一台电脑都能安全远程使用 DSH","id":"gh:1337429978","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-zen-remote","slug":"KyoMio/dsh-zen-remote","topics":["ai-agent","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","mobile","pwa","remote-access","remote-session","web-push"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Use DeepSeek Harness from your phone or another computer. Host: mobile UI, pairing-code gateway, PWA"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" and Web Push, plus sharing chosen sessions. Client: those sessions appear in another DSH desktop's "},{"id":"p1s3","text":"sidebar. 手机和另一台电脑都能安全远程使用 DSH"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"dsh-zen-remote\nOne DeepSeek Harness plugin, two roles. The host turns DSH into a phone-reachable PWA"},{"id":"p2s2","text":" (mobile UI, pairing gateway, lock-screen push) and shares chosen sessions to paired desktops. The c"},{"id":"p2s3","text":"lient runs inside another DSH desktop app and puts the host's shared sessions right into its own sid"},{"id":"p2s4","text":"ebar (up to 8 hosts connected simultaneously) — full history, live progress, messages, approvals, te"},{"id":"p2s5","text":"rminal, everything executes on the host."},{"id":"p3s1","text":"中文文档"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"| Session list home | Session page | Session info card |"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"| Composer permission sheet | Pairing page a public visitor sees |"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> Screenshots are a 390×844 phone viewport in the light theme; both themes are supported. The pairin"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"g page is drawn by the gateway in DSH's official style, following the system light / dark appearance"},{"id":"p6s3","text":" page is drawn by the gateway in DSH's official style, following the system light / dark appearance."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"1. Install\n2. Quick Start (Unified Setup & Pairing Wizard)\n- Scenario A: Set up as Host (Phone & Des"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ktop Access)\n- Scenario B: Set up as Desktop Client (Connect up to 8 Hosts)\n3. Daily Usage: Session "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"Sharing & Cross-Device Workflow\n4. Lock-Screen Push: When Notifications Fire\n5. Features\n6. Advanced"},{"id":"p8s4","text":" Settings & Field Reference\n7. Security Model, Version Tolerance & Known Notes"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## 1. Install"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### Install from the UI (Recommended, Desktop App & Web UI)"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Open the **Plugins** page in the DSH sidebar → click **Add plugin** → type `dsh-zen-remote` → click "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"**Enable now** when the install finishes, then restart the DSH desktop app (or `dsh web`)."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### Install from the CLI (Headless `dsh web` server)"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"> `dsh plugin` requires `--profile` to name the target profile. The desktop app's `desktop` profile "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"is managed exclusively by the app (`--profile desktop` is refused on the CLI), so use the UI install"},{"id":"p14s3","text":" above on the desktop app."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## 5. Features"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- **Mobile PWA UI (Host)**: two-level page stack (session list home + session page with swipe-back a"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"nd Android back-gesture support, first-frame boot skeleton, immutable asset caching), auto-discovere"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"d plugin entry chips, compact mobile composer with bottom sheets and phone attachment uploads, and a"},{"id":"p16s4","text":" session info card (6-tile stats with `tok/s` output speed, log export, rename, fork, archive, one-t"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"ap full-conversation PNG share image, and remote access switch).\n- **Unified Setup Wizard & Headless"},{"id":"p16s6","text":" CLI (`dsh-zen-remote`)**: top-of-page 2×2 live overview card, 3-step modal wizard, and a full-featu"},{"id":"p16s7","text":"red terminal CLI (`setup` / `status` / `host` / `client`) covering all four host ingress modes (Mana"},{"id":"p16s8","text":"ged Caddy, Existing Reverse Proxy, Cloudflare Tunnel, LAN / Tailscale Direct with private-IP wall) a"},{"id":"p16s9","text":"nd client pairing.\n- **Cross-Desktop Remote Sessions & Multi-Server Pool (Client)**: connect up to *"},{"id":"p16s10","text":"*8 main servers** simultaneously in pairing order; supports full history & live streaming, approval/"},{"id":"p16s11","text":"question sync, per-server isolated model catalog, file tree & Git diffs, duplex server-side terminal"},{"id":"p16s12","text":" (`terminal/attach`), inline Markdown image & media forwarding, windowed artifact downloads, server-"},{"id":"p16s13","text":"side LibreOffice PDF preview, up to 500 MiB file uploads (drag-and-drop, paperclip picker, and paste"},{"id":"p16s14","text":"), and one-click redacted diagnostics export.\n- **Plugin Bridge**: cooperative plugins and built-in "},{"id":"p16s15","text":"adapters (such as `dsh-better-sidebar` `0.25.0`–`0.30.1`) route their panel HTTP and WebSocket reque"},{"id":"p16s16","text":"sts in remote sessions to the host machine (with explicit owner consent for whole-machine data). See"},{"id":"p16s17","text":" Plugin Bridge Guide."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"In depth: Interface Design · Public Access & Relay Protocol"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## 7. Security Model, Version Tolerance & Known Notes"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- **Trusted client & strict session isolation**: a paired desktop client runs terminals and file pre"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"views as the host's OS user, while unshared sessions are strictly filtered and refused at the relay "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"layer. Even when binding `0.0.0.0` for LAN/Tailscale, the gateway's private-IP wall rejects any unpr"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"oxied public internet IP (`403 public-direct-forbidden`), and all admin/wizard mutations are restric"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"ted to the host machine itself.\n- **Version tolerance**: both ends must run the same `dsh-zen-remote"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"` version; DSH host versions may differ (interface fingerprints are compared at handshake and degrad"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"e only mismatched panels)."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Expand security & state-file details, known limitations, iOS PWA notes & adapted third-party plugins"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"**Data & state files**\n- The plugin reports nothing to any third party. Pairing state lives in `~/.d"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"sh/lan-gate-state.json`; the unified state file `~/.dsh/zen-remote-state.json` (`0600`) carries the "},{"id":"p21s3","text":"local `serverId`, the shared-session table `sessions`, and the client's paired servers list `servers"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"` (up to 8 servers, tokens included); Cloudflare tokens live in `0600` files under `~/.dsh/zen-remot"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"ervers, tokens included); Cloudflare tokens live in `0600` files under `~/.dsh/zen-remote-ingress/`."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"**Known limitations**\n- With multiple DSH windows open simultaneously on a client, active-session de"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"tection may occasionally dismiss a closed session early.\n- Switching between different servers or re"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"creating a workspace with the same ID requires reloading the client page once.\n- \"Export session\" an"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"d server-local OS dialogs (\"Reveal in Finder\" / \"Open in app\") are hidden in remote sessions.\n- DSH'"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"s own Settings RPCs are loopback-only by upstream design, so plugin settings must be edited on the m"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"achine running DSH rather than through a remote browser."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"**iOS standalone PWA notes**\n- **iOS 26.x viewport shrinkage**: home-screen PWAs may lose a status-b"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ar height at the bottom (an iOS WebKit bug); three mitigation layers are built in, and restarting th"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"e PWA restores full height.\n- **iOS 26+ top progressive blur**: opening from the home screen may sho"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"w a system `WKScrollPocket` blur across the top ~95px; entering any session and navigating back to t"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"llPocket` blur across the top ~95px; entering any session and navigating back to the list clears it."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
